              "text": "تنور (tanur) — \"a clay oven, a bread oven\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نان تازه را از تنور بیرون آورد. Nân-e tâze râ az tanur birun âvard. He took the fresh bread out of the clay oven."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A round oven of clay or sunk in the ground; nân-e tanuri \"oven bread\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tanur is inherited from Middle Persian tanūr, \"oven\" (EtymDB), an old word that EtymDB takes back to Akkadian; Arabic and Aramaic have it too."
            }
          ]
        },
